<</Type/StructElem/S/Figure/Alt(Two cumulative-hours lines over four years, 208 weeks. The sprinter's dashed line rises steeply to 300 hours by week 12, where it is marked burnout, and stays flat. The steady one's solid line rises six hours a week, crosses it at week 50, passes through the hatched job-ready band, 394 to 488 hours, in weeks 66 to 81, and reaches the outlined whole-book band, 957 to 1,193 hours, in year 4.)/P 91 0 R/Pg 52 0 R/K 36>>
